.TH SLKD 8 "2025-04-05" "SparkLink" "System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
slkd \- SparkLink wireless daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B slkd
.RB [ \-c
.IR config ]
.RB [ \-d
.IR device ]
.RB [ \-n ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B slkd
is the central management daemon for SparkLink wireless devices. It
communicates with the kernel SparkLink subsystem through the character device,
exposes a D\-Bus system bus interface for applications and CLI tools, manages
device discovery, connections, security, and SSAP services.
.PP
On startup the daemon opens the kernel device, loads bonding data from
.IR /var/lib/sparklink/ ,
connects to the system D\-Bus, and enters the event loop.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-c " path" "\fR,\fP \-\-config " path
Explicit path must be readable and valid; any error aborts startup. With no
option, the implicit default is:
.IR /etc/sparklink/main.conf .
See
.BR sparklink.conf (5).
.TP
.BI \-d " path" "\fR,\fP \-\-device " path
Kernel character device path. Default:
.IR /dev/sparklink .
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-nodetach
Run in foreground, do not daemonize. Useful for debugging and systemd
.BR Type=simple .
.SH D\-BUS INTERFACE
.B slkd
registers the well\-known name
.B org.sparklink
on the system bus and serves the following object paths:
.SS /org/sparklink (org.sparklink.Manager)
.TP
.B Version() \-> s
Return the daemon version string.
.TP
.B ListAdapters() \-> as
Return object paths of available adapters.
.SS /org/sparklink/slk0 (org.sparklink.Adapter)
.TP
.B StartDiscovery()
Begin scanning for nearby devices.
.TP
.B StopDiscovery()
Stop scanning.
.TP
.B ConnectDevice(s addr)
Initiate a connection to the device with the given hex address.
.TP
.B GetDevices() \-> a(ssqb)
Return a list of discovered devices. Each entry contains the address, name,
RSSI, and connected flag.
.PP
Properties:
.BR Powered " (b),"
.BR Discovering " (b),"
.BR Name " (s)."
.SS /org/sparklink/slk0/dev_{ADDR} (org.sparklink.Device)
.TP
.B Connect()
Connect to this device.
.TP
.B Disconnect()
Disconnect this device.
.PP
Properties:
.BR Address " (s),"
.BR Name " (s),"
.BR Rssi " (n),"
.BR Connected " (b),"
.BR DiscoveryLevel " (y)."
.SS /org/sparklink/slk0/security (org.sparklink.Security)
.TP
.B GetInfo() \-> (ssyb)
Return current security state, method, mode and encryption flag.
.TP
.B SetPsk(s hex)
Set a 16\-byte Pre\-Shared Key in hex.
.TP
.B Pair(s method)
Start pairing. Method: "just_works", "psk", or "none".
.TP
.B Encrypt()
Enable encryption on the active connection.
.TP
.B GetPasskey() \-> u
Return the displayed passkey for numeric comparison.
.TP
.B ConfirmPasskey() / RejectPasskey()
Accept or reject the passkey.
.TP
.B InputPasskey(u passkey)
Enter a 6\-digit passkey.
.TP
.B ListBonded() \-> as
Return addresses of all bonded devices.
.TP
.B RemoveBond(s addr)
Remove bonding information for the given device.
.TP
.B Reset()
Reset security state.
.PP
Properties:
.BR Encrypted " (b),"
.BR Paired " (b)."
.SS /org/sparklink/slk0/services (org.sparklink.ServiceManager)
.TP
.B RegisterServices(s json)
Register local SSAP services described in JSON.
.TP
.B AddService(q uuid, y type)
Add a single SSAP service.
.TP
.B AddProperty(q svc_handle, q uuid, y perms, ay data)
Add a property to a service.
.TP
.B ReadProperty(q handle) \-> ay
Read a property value.
.TP
.B WriteProperty(q handle, ay data)
Write a property value.
.TP
.B Notify(q handle, ay data)
Send a notification on a property.
.SS /org/sparklink/slk0/extadv (org.sparklink.ExtAdv)
.TP
.B Configure(y type, q interval, y txpower)
Configure an extended advertising instance.
.TP
.B SetData(y handle, ay data)
Set advertising data.
.TP
.B Enable(y handle) / Disable(y handle) / Remove(y handle)
Control advertising instances.
.TP
.B GetInfo(y handle) \-> (yyqy)
Get advertising instance information.
.SS /org/sparklink/slk0/controller (org.sparklink.Controller)
Provides low\-level controller access: role management, PHY/MCS configuration,
power management, AFH, connection statistics, DLI, measurement, sync link
control, resolving address list, and subsystem statistics. Approximately 40
methods; consult
.BR slctl (1)
for the corresponding CLI commands.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/sparklink/main.conf
Daemon configuration file. See
.BR sparklink.conf (5).
.TP
.I /dev/sparklink
Kernel driver character device.
.TP
.I /var/lib/sparklink/
Persistent bonding data directory.
.TP
.I /var/run/dbus/system_bus_socket
D\-Bus system bus socket.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGINT, SIGTERM
Graceful shutdown.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR slctl (1),
.BR sparklink.conf (5),
.BR dbus\-daemon (1)
